  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/527864": {
      "title": "Staff Accountant",
      "description": "Staff Accountant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Staff Accountant Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description Rockhurst University is currently seeking a Staff Accountant to join our Finance Office. The Staff Accountant performs a variety of professional accounting work related to the preparation and maintenance of accounting and financial reporting records and financial functions related to budget and annual audits. The position requires knowledge of fund accounting, independent judgement and decision-making skills. Duties will include journal entries, reconciliations, monthly and annual close processes, financial reporting, and audit and compliance support. Duties include daily, monthly, and annual accounting functions. Responsible for providing financial information to the VPFA, Controller, departments, grant managers/writer, board and committee members, and other related duties as assigned within the scope of the classification level. Staff Accountant is the mid-level class in the professional accounting series. Initially, under close supervision, incumbents perform the more routine accounting duties while learning policies and procedures and becoming familiar with a variety of departmental systems and practices. As experience is gained, duties become more diversified and are performed under more general supervision. Specific responsibilities include: General Ledger & journal entries – prepare and post standard monthly journal entries and maintain general ledger accounts. Account reconciliations – perform monthly balance sheet, bank, and other payment reconciliations Month-end close – assist with month-end, quarter-end, and year-end closing procedures, including accruals and adjustments. Financial reporting support – support the compilation of financial statements, variance analysis, and management reports. Audit – provide supporting documentation and schedules and answer questions during internal and external audits. Compliance – ensure transactions and reports follow company policies and standard accounting regulations. Other duties as assigned – perform other duties, consistent with the incumbent’s skills and qualifications as required by the University in support of the department. Position requirements include: Possession of a bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university, with major course work in accounting, finance, business administration, or a closely related field with two years working experience. Two years of accounting experience with knowledge of Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable and General Ledger as well as general office operations. Exceptional organizational skills with strong attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines Comfortable working independently and collaboratively. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work with people from diverse backgrounds. Commitment to providing excellent customer service. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications. Experience with databases and data management. Full-time Rockhurst employees enjoy an excellent benefits package including: Medical Dental Vision Short- and long-term disability Life insurance A 37.5-hour work week Free undergraduate and graduate classes for employees - 6 credit hour limit per semester Free undergraduate classes for spouses and dependent children Vacation and sick time along with 15 paid holidays Positive work environment Leadership and development opportunities Founded by the Jesuits in 1910, Rockhurst is a comprehensive university of 3000 students that offers more than fifty undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs taught by nationally recognized faculty. Rockhurst emphasizes learning, leadership, and service. Our mission is to transform lives by creating a learning community centered on excellence in undergraduate liberal and graduate education. Rockhurst is Catholic and Jesuit, involved in the life and growth of the city and the region, and committed to the service of the contemporary world. We employ approximately 500 faculty and staff. DISCLAIMER: The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification. It is not designed to contain, nor is it to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. The application process requires a cover letter, salary requirements, and contact information for three references. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. In order to qualify as a candidate, you must be legally authorized to work in the United States. At this time Rockhurst is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/521742": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology - Tenure Track You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Biology - Tenure Track Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description The Biology Department of Rockhurst University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Biology position. This is a full-time, 9-month position to begin in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching primarily a combination of lecture and laboratory courses in General Biology, maintaining an active discipline-based research program, and participating in departmental and university service. A PhD in Biology or related field is required for this position. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. As Kansas City’s Jesuit university, Rockhurst University exemplifies all that Jesuit education has to offer, an academic tradition that dates back nearly 500 years. The highest caliber of academia, leadership, and service to others is the foundation in which we build a transformative experience for students. The beautiful 55-acre campus is centrally located in a thriving metropolis with a diverse population of more than 2 million people. Kansas City has been ranked among the top 50 best places to live in the United States. The Jesuit tradition engages students in integrating knowledge, critical analysis, and personal reflection that prepares students to be compassionate, just, and globally aware leaders in a diverse and ever-changing world. Rockhurst is a comprehensive university offering more than 50 undergraduate and graduate programs taught by nationally recognized faculty. The position offers a full benefits package. For best consideration, please apply through our online system. Review will continue until filled. Applicants should submit an online application including: (1) a letter of interest which includes demonstration of job qualifications (2) curriculum vitae, and (3) names and contact information for three references. All material should be in one document. Unofficial transcripts will be required of those selected for on-campus interviews before the on-campus interview. Inquiries should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Lisa Felzien, lisa.felzien@rockhurst.edu. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Questions about submitting applications through our online system can be directed to our Human Resources office at 816-501-4835. The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification. It is not designed to contain, or it is to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
