    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/513871": {
      "title": "Director of Ignatian Spirituality Center",
      "description": "Director of Ignatian Spirituality Center You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Ignatian Spirituality Center Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description Rockhurst University is looking for a dynamic, faith-filled team member to serve as Director of the Ignatian Spirituality Center. Founded by the Jesuits in 1910 and located in Kansas City, Missouri, Rockhurst is a comprehensive university of nearly 3,500 students that offers more than fifty undergraduate, master, and doctoral programs taught by nationally recognized faculty. Our mission is to form lifelong learners in the Catholic, Jesuit, liberal arts tradition who engage with the complexities of our world and serve others as compassionate, thoughtful leaders. Rockhurst is committed to creating a more just world through inclusive, innovative, and transformative education. Reporting to the VP for Mission & Ministry, the full-time Director of the Ignatian Spirituality Center is responsible for providing strategic, spiritual, apostolic, and operational leadership for the Center and serving as the primary steward of its mission, programs, partnerships, volunteer ministry community, and organizational sustainability. The Director works collaboratively with the ISC Advisory Board and the Center’s core volunteer committees – including Program, Guide Formation, and Applications – in sustaining the mission, discernment, and apostolic life of the Center. Thus, this is a highly relational leadership role requiring pastoral presence, strong organizational leadership, strategic vision, and the ability to inspire and sustain a vibrant community of retreatants, spiritual directors, volunteers, donors, and institutional partners. The Director will ensure that the Spiritual Exercises in Everyday Life remain the Center’s primary mission and that the Center continues to serve the wider Kansas City community through a strong, volunteer-led ministry of trained prayer guides. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: · Provide strategic and spiritual leadership for the Ignatian Spirituality Center and its apostolic mission · Oversee retreats, formation programs, spiritual accompaniment initiatives, and apostolic partnerships · Support and sustain volunteer spiritual guide formation and lay apostolic leadership · Foster strong relationships with Jesuit, ecclesial, civic, and university partners · Provide operational oversight including budgeting, communications, advancement collaboration, marketing, assessment, and planning · Collaborate with the ISC Advisory Board and core committees in sustaining the mission and life of the Center · Support faculty and staff formation initiatives connected to Ignatian spirituality and Jesuit mission of Rockhurst University · Represent the Center and the University within Ignatian and Jesuit networks and partnerships · Perform other duties as assigned consistently with the mission and responsibilities of the position Position Requirements · Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree in theology, ministry, spirituality, higher education, nonprofit leadership, or related field strongly preferred · Completion of the full Spiritual Exercises of St. Ignatius Loyola · Demonstrated knowledge of Ignatian spirituality, Jesuit mission, Catholic spiritual tradition, and an openness to engage in ecumenical relationships · Five or more years of experience in spiritual formation, retreat ministry, pastoral leadership, higher education, nonprofit leadership, or related fields · Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with diverse constituencies including volunteers, clergy, faculty, administrators, benefactors, and community partners · Strong organizational, strategic planning, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills · Ability to provide pastoral leadership and spiritual accompaniment within a diverse community · Commitment to the Catholic, Jesuit, and Ignatian traditions of Rockhurst University and the Ignatian Spirituality Center Preferred Qualifications · Experience working within Jesuit institutions or apostolic ministries · Experience supporting volunteer leadership and advisory board governance · Familiarity with fundraising, advancement, and mission-centered communications · Experience with strategic planning, organizational leadership, and program assessment · Experience coordinating retreats, spiritual formation programs, or adult faith formation initiatives · Ability to build relationships with the Catholic community and other Christian denominations Interested candidates should apply with a cover letter which includes salary requirements, a resume, and contact information for three professional references. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Review of applications will begin the week of September 14 and continue until the position is filled. Rockhurst University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. Rockhurst University uses E-Verify. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/509175": {
      "title": "CRNA Program Director",
      "description": "CRNA Program Director You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account CRNA Program Director Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description Rockhurst University, College of Nursing and Health Sciences is seeking applicants for an experienced and Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA) to join us as the founding Program Director. This individual will lead the design, development, and implementation of a jointly offered nurse anesthetist program. The Program Director will guide the university partnership to achieve accreditation and build infrastructure for a successful launch. The Program Director will leverage their expertise in nurse anesthesia education and accreditation standards to create a comprehensive, high-quality program that meets the needs of students, faculty, and stakeholders. Rockhurst is a welcoming and inclusive private Catholic, Jesuit institution with a strong mission aligned with the core values of nursing. The College of Nursing is in one of two academic schools housed in Saint Luke’s College of Nursing and Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is known for its innovative teaching using a broad range of active learning experiences, close faculty-student interactions, and our strong mission focused on service, advocacy, and leadership. The faculty have established close relationships with many community partners, enabling community-based service learning for students and clinical practice opportunities for students and faculty. Rockhurst nursing students often receive commendations for excellence in academics, professionalism, commitment to social justice, and leadership. Additional details about the Nursing Program are available on the program's website: https://www.rockhurst.edu/saint-lukes-college. Overall Duties and Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Program Design and Development: Develop a curriculum for the nurse anesthetist program, aligning it with the standards of the Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs (COA). Design coursework, clinical training requirements, and evaluation methods to ensure program excellence. Incorporate best practices in CRNA education and nurse anesthesia to create a rigorous and engaging program. Accreditation Preparation: Prepare and submit the documentation and applications to achieve program accreditation through the COA accrediting body. Coordinate planning with university administration to support review and approval by the Higher Learning Commission. Conduct a gap analysis of current resources and recommend solutions to meet accreditation requirements. Coordinate accreditation-related activities, ensuring compliance with all standards. Resource Development: Identify and recommend facilities, technology, and resources to support program operations. Assist in recruiting and onboarding qualified faculty and staff to deliver the program. Support faculty with the development of coursework and clinical experiences to achieve learning outcomes. Quality Assurance and Continuous Improvement: Establish metrics and evaluation tools to assess program effectiveness and student outcomes. Provide recommendations for ongoing program improvements to maintain accreditation standards and ensure graduate success. Position Requirements: · Current certification as a Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA). · Earned doctorate. · Extensive knowledge of nurse anesthesia program accreditation standards and processes. · Proven experience in program design, curriculum development, and accreditation. · Strong organizational, analytical, and project management skills. · Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to engage with diverse stakeholders. Preferred Experience: · Prior experience consulting or leading new program development in higher education. · Familiarity with clinical site partnerships and clinical training program implementation. · Demonstrated success in achieving accreditation for a nurse anesthetist or healthcare-related program. Applicants should submit a cover letter with salary expectations and three professional references. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. DISCLAIMER: The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification. It is not designed to contain, nor is it to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. In order to qualify as a candidate, you must be legally authorized to work in the United States. At this time Rockhurst is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/507345": {
      "title": "Clinical Nursing Instructor",
      "description": "Clinical Nursing Instructor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Clinical Nursing Instructor Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description Rockhurst University is seeking a Clinical Nursing Instructor. Rockhurst is a welcoming and inclusive private Catholic, Jesuit institution with a strong mission aligned with the core values of nursing. The College of Nursing is in one of two academic schools housed in Saint Luke’s College of Nursing and Health Sciences. The College of Nursing is known for its innovative teaching using a broad range of active learning experiences, close faculty-student interactions, and our strong mission focused on service, advocacy, and leadership. The faculty have established close relationships with many community partners, enabling community-based service learning for students and clinical practice opportunities for students and faculty. Rockhurst nursing students often receive commendations for excellence in academics, professionalism, commitment to social justice, and leadership. Additional details about the Nursing Program are available on the program's website: https://www.rockhurst.edu/saint-lukes-college This position will serve as a BSN faculty member, primarily teaching clinicals, immersions, and simulation experiences. It will report directly to the BSN and ABSN Program Directors and collaborate closely with the Clinical Lead. Responsibilities include: Preparing courses/ clinical/ simulation/ lab outlines and syllabi in collaboration with the course lead and track coordinator, developing content and lesson plans, and engaging in the selection of textbooks and other teaching aids necessary for the instruction of courses/ clinical/ simulation/ lab. Conduct instruction for courses in the nursing curriculum at a higher education level utilizing diverse teaching strategies. Teach pertinent subject matter using lectures, demonstrations, class discussions, clinicals, labs, simulations, and other appropriate modes of educational delivery in the face-to-face, online, and/or hybrid environment. Develop and maintain relationships with clinical partners. Participate in co-curricular activities such as department colloquia as needed. Serve as an informal academic advisor/mentor to students and foster their personal and professional development. Position Requirements: · Minimum of an MSN degree. · 2-5 years of nursing experience required · Terminal degree preferred. · Strong organizational, analytical, planning, interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills. · Ability to interact professionally with a diverse group of individuals. · Effective project management skills; detail and deadline oriented. Applicants should submit a cover letter with salary expectations, Curriculum Vitae and three professional references. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Rockhurst University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/507315": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Speech Language Pathology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Speech Language Pathology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Speech Language Pathology Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description Rockhurst University's Department of Speech-Language Pathology invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Speech-Language Pathology position. This is a full-time, 11-month, tenure-track position to begin January 2027. Responsibilities include preparing and teaching course material in the SLP curriculum at a higher education level, covering pertinent subject matter using lectures, demonstrations, class discussions, practicums, labs, simulations, and other appropriate modes of educational delivery, as well as conducting and mentoring research in areas of expertise. This position is not remote. The position requires strong organizational and technological skills, as data management is a key responsibility. The incumbent must be able to submit student progress reports and attendance in a timely fashion. Collaborative skills are also a necessity, as the incumbent must work with academic and interpersonal partners while also adhering to all Saint Luke’s College of Nursing and Health Sciences and Rockhurst policies and procedures to properly facilitate student learning. Most importantly, the job must support and contribute to the mission of the department through service commiserate with rank and experience. Accountabilities 1. Prepare course/practicum/lab outlines and syllabi in collaboration with the Program Director and Chair, develop content and lesson plans, and select textbooks and other teaching aids necessary for the instruction of courses/practicums/labs. 2. Conduct instruction of courses in the SLP curriculum at a higher education level utilizing diverse teaching strategies. 3. Teach pertinent subject matter using lectures, demonstrations, class discussions, practicums, labs, simulations, and other appropriate modes of educational delivery in the face-to-face, online, and/or hybrid environment. 4. Effectively collaborate with academic and interprofessional partners to facilitate student learning in various settings, including classroom, clinical lab, and simulation. 5. Conduct research in area(s) of expertise and mentor students in research and service activities. 6. Submits student progress reports and attendance to the Program Director and Academic Advisor and discusses any student needs that may require directed attention or remediation plans. Position Requirements · Research doctorate (EdD or PhD) in speech-language pathology · At least three years of professional experience · Prior experience in teaching and course development for hybrid and online courses · Record of scholarly contributions to the SLP field · Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues in a university setting · Alignment with the mission of Rockhurst University · ASHA Certification (CCC-SLP) · State licensure (or eligibility) in speech-language pathology Located in the heart of Kansas City, the Rockhurst CSD Department has a 20-year history of excellence in scholarly, academic, and clinical preparation of students. Community partnerships are at the heart of this well-established program where students gain clinical skills in real-world environments. The Rockhurst CSD program offers a variety of course modalities with potential for innovation. Additional information may be found here: https://www.rockhurst.edu/slp As Kansas City's Jesuit university, Rockhurst University exemplifies all that Jesuit education has to offer, an academic tradition that dates back nearly 500 years. The highest caliber of academia, leadership, and service to others is the foundation on which we build a transformative experience for students. The beautiful 55-acre campus is centrally located in a thriving metropolis with a diverse population of more than 2 million people. Kansas City has been ranked among the top 50 best places to live in the United States. DISCLAIMER: The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification. It is not designed to contain, nor is it to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. In order to qualify as a candidate, you must be legally authorized to work in the United States. At this time Rockhurst is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/481379": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Education You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Education Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description Rockhurst University's School of Education invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Education position. This is an 11-month, tenure-track position with a start date of January 4, 2027 . Responsibilities include teaching doctoral courses and supervising doctoral students’ research projects as well as supporting undergraduate and graduate-level teacher candidates. Applicants must have demonstrated an active research agenda. A specialization in areas pertaining to Special Education or Teacher Education is preferred. The School of Education supports undergraduate educator preparation programs, graduate certificates, Master of Education programs, and EdD in Education and Leadership programs. Graduate programs are delivered using online modalities and the Ed.D. in Education and Leadership is an online, cohort-based program with four concentration areas: K-12 Education, Higher Education, Healthcare Education, and Organizational Leadership. This Jesuit - inspired Ed.D. program provides a distinctive approach to developing educational leaders and health care educators prepared to face the challenges of todays accelerated rate of change. The faculty teaching load will include courses such as Foundations of Special Education, Research Methodology I and II, and Research Capstone I and II. The tenure-track faculty member will engage in scholarship activities; provide service to the university, department, program, and community; and advise and mentor students. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. or Ed.D. in curriculum and instruction, special education, educational leadership, or closely related discipline Excellent oral and written communication and interpersonal skills Evidence of teaching excellence in higher education Evidence of an on-going scholarly agenda Experience with directing graduate student research experiences Experience with advising students Experience with course development, implementation, and assessment Preferred Qualifications A minimum of three years of experience teaching at the college level Innovative pedagogy, including online teaching and learning practices Research interests in fields such as special education, teacher education, health care education, or education administration / leadership Expertise in quantitative and qualitative research methods An awareness of and interest in the educational mission of Jesuit higher education Evidence of demonstrated commitment to teaching and mentoring graduate students from underrepresented backgrounds Salary is commensurate with skills and experience. The position offers a full benefits package. As Kansas City's Jesuit university, Rockhurst University exemplifies all that Jesuit education has to offer, an academic tradition that dates back nearly 500 years. The highest caliber of academia, leadership, and service to others is the foundation on which we build a transformative experience for students. The beautiful 55-acre campus is centrally located in a thriving metropolis with a diverse population of more than 2 million people. Kansas City has been ranked among the top 50 best places to live in the United States. For best consideration, please apply through our online system by September 15, 2026. Review will continue until filled. Applicants should submit an online application including: (1) a letter of interest which includes demonstration of job qualifications and a brief description of your teaching philosophy (2) curriculum vitae, (3) research interests and agenda, and (4) names and contact information for three references. Items 1-3 need to be scanned and submitted as one file upload in the questions portion of the application. Unofficial transcripts will be required of those selected for on-campus interviews before the on-campus interviews. Inquiries should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Sarah Hicks sarah.hicks@rockhurst.edu . Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Questions about submitting applications through our online system can be directed to our Human Resources office at 816-501-4087. DISCLAIMER: The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification.  It is not designed to contain, nor is it to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. In order to qualify as a candidate, you must be legally authorized to work in the United States. At this time Rockhurst is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/476583": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Architecture and Program Director",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Architecture and Program Director You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Architecture and Program Director Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description Rockhurst University and the College of Arts and Sciences is hiring a tenure-track or non-tenure-track faculty member in Architecture to start in Fall, 2027. In Fall 2028, Rockhurst will begin a Bachelor’s of Science in Architectural Studies (unaccredited) which will lead to a Master of Architecture, for which we will seek NAAB accreditation. We seek a creative and dynamic faculty member and program director for this program. This position will have a formative role in shaping the program. The successful candidate will be responsible for developing and promoting a new program that is grounded in ethics and quantitative reasoning. Our Architecture program will embrace the Jesuit tradition of pedagogy, which is holistic and grounded in the liberal arts. The candidate will teach studio courses and other courses in architecture; develop the architecture curriculum; participate in the accreditation process; mentor students; build external connections with architecture firms; promote the program. The successful candidate will have a professional degree in Architecture and licensure as an architect, with a minimum of four years of professional experience. Founded by the Jesuits in 1910, Rockhurst is a comprehensive university that offers more than fifty undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs taught by nationally recognized faculty. Essential functions of this role include: Teach pertinent course subject matter using lectures, studios, class discussions, and other appropriate modes of educational delivery. Prepare course outline and syllabus, develop course and lesson plans, and engage in the selection of textbook and other teaching aids necessary to the instruction of courses; Conduct course instruction for one or more courses in the curriculum at the higher education level utilizing diverse teaching strategies, to include posting and grading on Rockhurst learning management system software; Produce peer-reviewed scholarship in their disciplinary field; Collect student assessment data in preparation for accreditation; Interact with the RU Architecture Advisory Board; Develop connections with high schools and community colleges; Serve as an academic advisor to students, and foster students’ personal and professional development. May also supervise independent study and individualized instruction as planned and approved with the collaboration of the Academic Dean. Create new and revise existing courses and programs using current evidence-based practice. Attend and participate in all college meetings, departmental meetings, committee meetings, graduations and other such gatherings as required of faculty members. Provide service to the program, college, university and/or other constituents commensurate of one’s rank, through committee involvement and/or leadership. Position requirements: A doctorate is required for tenure-track status; a master’s degree will be considered for a non-tenure-track position; A research and teaching focus in a field of architecture is required; Evidence of scholarly and creative ability; Prior teaching experience in higher education preferred; Evidence of commitment to scholarly work, service and teaching; Ability to work independently as well as a part of a team professionally and confidentially. DISCLAIMER: The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification. It is not designed to contain, nor is it to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. The application process requires a cover letter, salary requirements, and contact information for three references. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. In order to qualify as a candidate, you must be legally authorized to work in the United States. At this time Rockhurst is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
