    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/373112": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator and Clinical Assistant Professor of Information Systems",
      "description": "Program Coordinator and Clinical Assistant Professor of Information Systems You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Program Coordinator and Clinical Assistant Professor of Information Systems Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description The Department of Math, Analytics, and Technology in the College of Business and Technology at Rockhurst University invites applications for a full-time Program Coordinator and Clinical Assistant Professor of Information Systems. This unique position combines teaching and leadership responsibilities in a dynamic, interdisciplinary environment. The successful candidate will help shape the future of our graduate and undergraduate technology programs through innovative instruction, strategic program development, and industry engagement. Position Overview This role involves a dual appointment: - Teaching: Deliver undergraduate and graduate courses in information systems and related subjects using lectures, demonstrations, discussions, and other appropriate modes of educational delivery. - Program Coordination: The Program Coordinator will support the academic development of the Master of Science in Information Systems (MSIS) program, with collaborative involvement in related programs such as the Bachelor of Science in Computer Science and Bachelor of Science in Cybersecurity. While the Technology Program Director oversees administrative functions—including university partnerships and strategic alignment—the Program Coordinator will focus on subject matter leadership, including curriculum development, student recruitment, academic advising, and industry engagement. This role reports directly to the Technology Program Director and works closely with faculty and staff to ensure that program content remains current, relevant, and aligned with college goals and industry needs. About Rockhurst University Founded in 1910 and located in the heart of Kansas City, Missouri, Rockhurst is a Catholic university in the Jesuit tradition committed to inclusive, innovative, and transformative education. As a comprehensive university serving nearly 4,000 students, our mission is to form lifelong learners in the liberal arts tradition who engage the complexities of our world and serve others as compassionate, thoughtful leaders. Qualifications Education & Experience - Master’s degree in information systems, computer science, information technology, cybersecurity, or a related discipline (required). - Minimum of 8 years of progressive leadership experience in IT, cybersecurity, software engineering, or related fields. - Proven track record in senior IT leadership roles (e.g., CIO, CTO, CISO, Director of Technology, IT Operations, Enterprise Architecture). Technical Expertise - Familiarity with modern enterprise and emerging technologies, including cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure), cybersecurity tools and frameworks, and software development practices (e.g., Python, Git, DevOps). - Ability to translate industry trends into educational experiences. Leadership & Collaboration - Experience building relationships with external partners, advisory boards, or professional associations. - Strong organizational and leadership abilities with a proactive approach to problem-solving and program development. - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to engage diverse stakeholders. Teaching & Scholarship - Prior teaching experience in higher education (preferred). - Evidence of scholarly and creative ability. - Commitment to service, teaching, and the technology industry. - Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a professional and confidential manner. Commitment to Values - Dedication to fostering diversity, equity, and inclusion in academia and the broader community. Additional Information - This is a full-time, non-tenure-track clinical faculty position with a renewable annual contract. - Expected teaching load is approximately 21 hours per academic year, which equals 3-4 classes per semester, with potential course release for administrative duties. - Opportunities for professional development and industry engagement are supported. Application Instructions Applicants should submit the following materials via Rockhurst’s online application system: - Cover letter including salary expectations - Curriculum Vitae - Three professional references Please note: Rockhurst cannot accept application materials via email, mail, or walk-in. All materials must be submitted through our online application system. Equal Employment Opportunity Rockhurst University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. Rockhurst uses E-Verify. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/370096": {
      "title": "English Adjunct",
      "description": "English Adjunct You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account English Adjunct Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description The English Department at Rockhurst University is looking for adjunct faculty to teach freshman composition in an in-person classroom setting.. Founded in 1910 and located in the heart of Kansas City, Missouri, Rockhurst is a Catholic university in the Jesuit tradition committed to providing inclusive, innovative, and transformative education. As a comprehensive university and supportive community of nearly 4,000 students, our mission is to form lifelong learners in the liberal arts tradition who engage the complexities of our world and serve others as compassionate, thoughtful leaders. Applicants must have a Master’s degree or PhD in English or creative writing and must be committed to the student-centered teaching of writing, teaching that is aimed at helping students develop as critical thinkers and proficient writers. The application process requires a cover letter and curriculum vitae, to be uploaded as one file submission.  Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Rockhurst University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. Rockhurst uses E-Verify. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
