    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/354451": {
      "title": "Chemistry Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Chemistry Adjunct Instructor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Chemistry Adjunct Instructor Hot Job Apply Apply Description The Chemistry Department at Rockhurst University is seeking adjunct instructors to teach undergraduate laboratory sections for the following courses: General Chemistry I and II Principles of General Chemistry Organic Chemistry I and II Applicants must have at least a master’s degree in chemistry, biochemistry, chemical education, or a closely related discipline, or a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in chemistry or a closely related field. A Ph.D. in chemistry or a related field is preferred. Prior college teaching experience is also preferred. This position is an in-person, part-time role. The application process requires a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Interested applicants should contact Dr. Michael Marvin, Chair of the Chemistry Department, at Michael.Marvin@rockhurst.edu. All applications and materials must be submitted through Rockhurst’s online application system. Rockhurst University provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
