    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/110847": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Physics",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Physics You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of Physics Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Apply Description The Physics and Engineering Department at Rockhurst University is seeking an adjunct instructor to teach undergraduate Introductory Physics for the Life Sciences (IPLS) lectures and laboratories. Curriculum will be provided and standardized across life science sections. Requirements: Applicants must have a master’s degree in physics, physics education, engineering or 18 Graduate credit hours in physics or closely related discipline. Prior college teaching experience is preferred. This adjunct position is face-to-face, part-time. The application process requires a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Interested applicants should contact Michael Marvin, Chair of the Physics and Engineering Department at Michael.Marvin@rockhurst.edu. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
