    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/531283": {
      "title": "Web Content Specialist",
      "description": "Web Content Specialist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Web Content Specialist Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description Rockhurst University is seeking a Web Content Specialist to join our Marketing Department. The Web Content Specialist is primarily responsible for writing, updating, and optimizing web content for Rockhurst University’s higher education website and related digital properties. This position reports to and assists the Director of Digital Media with all website governance and ensures the site’s content aligns with established web governance policies and style guidelines. This is a full-time, exempt, 12-month staff position. The role translates internal client needs into high-quality, brand-aligned digital content optimized for search engines (SEO) and AI-driven discovery (AIO). The specialist works closely with marketing and campus partners to maintain a consistent voice and ensure web content supports institutional goals. The ideal candidate excels in a high-velocity environment, managing competing deadlines while remaining receptive to editorial oversight and strategic feedback. Accountabilities (these are the ‘big picture’ responsibilities that the employee is accountable for) Create, update, and optimize web pages that support Rockhurst University’s digital strategy and overall web presence, including daily web content requests from a diverse campus client base Ensure web content supports search visibility, AI-driven discovery (AIO), accessibility standards, evolving digital best practices, and is tailored to most current requirements for SEO, AIO and evolving digital best practices Conduct routine website content audits to identify outdated content, repair broken links, and maintain streamlined, user-centered sitemap Update website on Drupal CMS Identify opportunities to improve website functionality, user experience (UX), performance, accessibility, and adherence to web standards Monitor web analytics in GA4 and create reports to help inform director and AVP and determine improvements Collaborate with marketing team members to implement strategies that improve digital marketing and advertising performance Other duties as Assigned – perform other duties, consistent with the incumbent’s skills and qualifications as required by the University in support of the department Position requirements include: Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, English, computer science, or a related field Two or more years of professional experience managing websites or digital content Experience working with a content management system (CMS); Drupal experience preferred Strong understanding of search engine optimization (SEO), AI-driven search discovery (AIO), accessibility standards, basic HTML, and analytics Full-time Rockhurst employees enjoy an excellent benefits package including: Medical Dental Vision Short- and long-term disability Life insurance A 37.5-hour work week Free undergraduate and graduate classes for employees - 6 credit hour limit per semester Free undergraduate classes for spouses and dependent children Vacation and sick time along with 15 paid holidays Positive work environment Leadership and development opportunities Founded by the Jesuits in 1910, Rockhurst is a comprehensive university of 3000 students that offers more than fifty undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs taught by nationally recognized faculty.  Rockhurst emphasizes learning, leadership, and service.  Our mission is to transform lives by creating a learning community centered on excellence in undergraduate liberal and graduate education.  Rockhurst is Catholic and Jesuit, involved in the life and growth of the city and the region, and committed to the service of the contemporary world.  We employ approximately 500 faculty and staff. DISCLAIMER: The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification.  It is not designed to contain, nor is it to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. The application process requires a cover letter, salary requirements, and contact information for three references. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. In order to qualify as a candidate, you must be legally authorized to work in the United States. At this time Rockhurst is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/531252": {
      "title": "University Assessment Coordinator & Title III Project Coordinator",
      "description": "University Assessment Coordinator & Title III Project Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account University Assessment Coordinator & Title III Project Coordinator Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description Rockhurst University is currently seeking a University Assessment Coordinator & Title III Project Coordinator to join our Office of Institutional Effectiveness. This position provides leadership in university academic assessment and federally funded Title III programs. This position is responsible for coordinating university-wide assessment initiatives; leading the university’s program review process; leading the university assessment committee of academic and co-curricular programs; providing oversight of the university course survey process, managing the university’s system for annual faculty evaluation, program assessment, strategic plan evaluation; ensuring alignment with HLC Criteria for Accreditation standards associated with assessment and program review; and managing the planning, implementation, and reporting of Title III grant-funded activities. The role supports continuous improvement in student learning outcomes and institutional performance while ensuring adherence to federal regulations and grant objectives. This is a full-time, exempt, 12-month staff position. This position reports directly to the Director of Institutional Effectiveness and indirectly to the Vice Provost for University Assessment items, and directly to the Vice Provost for items related to the Title III Grant. This position generally has no direct supervisory responsibility outside of supervision of federal work-study students as needed. Essential Functions Assessment Coordination Lead the coordination and continuous improvement of institutional assessment processes in alignment with HLC Criteria for Accreditation. Partner with academic programs and administrative units to develop measurable student learning outcomes (SLOs) and operational effectiveness metrics. Ensure systematic collection, analysis, and use of assessment data to demonstrate improvement in student learning and institutional performance. Prepare documentation and reports supporting: HLC accreditation reviews and assurance arguments Program review processes Institutional effectiveness reporting tied to assessment, accreditation, and program review Maintain and oversee Watermark, which is the university’s assessment management system, annual faculty evaluation system, course survey system, and program review management system Provide training, workshops, and consultation to faculty and staff on best practices in assessment and continuous quality improvement. Lead the university’s program review process and course survey process. Lead the university’s committee on assessment. Support integration of assessment findings into strategic planning and budgeting processes. Support survey creation by departments and other areas of the university as needed. Work collaboratively with eLearning and the Center for Excellence Teaching and Learning to facilitate effective teaching, learning, assessment across courses, programs, and co-curricular experiences. Title III Project Coordination Coordinate the implementation of Rockhurst University’s Title III grant programs, supporting initiatives that enhance student success, retention, and institutional capacity. Ensure compliance with U.S. Department of Education Title III regulations, grant guidelines, and reporting requirements. Provide oversight into the summer bridge program. Develop and monitor: Project timelines and milestones Performance indicators and measurable outcomes Program evaluation plans Advertising, marketing, and social media exposure associated with the grant and grant activities Collaborate with campus stakeholders to execute grant-funded activities, including academic support initiatives, faculty and staff development, and technology enhancements. Track budgets and expenditures in coordination with the Finance Office, ensuring responsible stewardship of federal funds. Prepare and submit required reports, including: Annual Performance Reports (APR) Interim and final grant reports Support long-term sustainability of grant-funded initiatives beyond the funding period. Work directly with the external evaluator on formative and annual summative evaluation of the Title III grant implementation. Participate in, and present at, appropriate conferences. Position requirements include: Master’s degree in the Behavioral Sciences, Higher Education, Education, Public Administration, Public Health, or related field. Minimum of 3 years of experience in higher education assessment, institutional effectiveness, or grant management. Demonstrated knowledge of Higher Learning Commission (HLC) accreditation standards and processes. Experience managing or supporting federally funded grants, preferably Title III. Strong analytical skills with experience interpreting and using data to drive improvements. Excellent written communication skills, particularly in preparing formal reports and accreditation documentation. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate in a relevant field. Experience at a Jesuit or mission-driven institution. Familiarity with assessment management systems (e.g., Watermark). Experience with program evaluation methodologies and data visualization tools. Knowledge of student success initiatives, equity-focused programming, and retention strategies. Full-time Rockhurst employees enjoy an excellent benefits package including: Medical Dental Vision Short- and long-term disability Life insurance A 37.5-hour work week Free undergraduate and graduate classes for employees - 6 credit hour limit per semester Free undergraduate classes for spouses and dependent children Vacation and sick time along with 15 paid holidays Positive work environment Leadership and development opportunities Founded by the Jesuits in 1910, Rockhurst is a comprehensive university of 3000 students that offers more than fifty undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs taught by nationally recognized faculty.  Rockhurst emphasizes learning, leadership, and service.  Our mission is to transform lives by creating a learning community centered on excellence in undergraduate liberal and graduate education.  Rockhurst is Catholic and Jesuit, involved in the life and growth of the city and the region, and committed to the service of the contemporary world.  We employ approximately 500 faculty and staff. DISCLAIMER: The information presented indicates the general nature and level of work expected of employees in this classification.  It is not designed to contain, nor is it to be interpreted as, a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, qualifications, and objectives required of employees assigned to this job. The application process requires a cover letter, salary requirements, and contact information for three references. Rockhurst cannot accept any application materials (resumes, cover letters, etc.) by email, mail, or walk-in. All applications and application materials must be submitted through our online application system. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rockhurst University is committed to creating a diverse working environment. The University recruits and employs successful candidates without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and/or disability in employment, educational programs, or activities that it operates. In order to qualify as a candidate, you must be legally authorized to work in the United States. At this time Rockhurst is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/76B960DE16E1EABF6B6D63157F84F11F/jobs/532502": {
      "title": "Patrol Officer",
      "description": "Patrol Officer You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Patrol Officer Hot Job Rockhurst University - Kansas City, MO 64110 Apply Overview Salary Range $22.25 Apply Description Security Patrol Officer (Armed/Evening/Overnight Shift) Department of Safety & Security | Rockhurst University Location : Kansas City, MO Pay : $22.25 / hour (Minimum $46,280 / year) Job Type : Full-Time Why Join Rockhurst University? At Rockhurst University, you are more than a security officer—you are a vital part of a close-knit, supportive campus community. We offer a progressive work environment focused on Community-Oriented Policing, professional growth, and an incredible rewards package. Unmatched Benefits Highlights: Medical Dental Vision Short- and long-term disability (100% Employer funded) Life insurance (100% Employer funded) Tuition assistance for undergraduate and graduate classes for employees - 6 credit hour limit per semester Tuition assistance for undergraduate classes for spouses and dependent children Vacation and sick time along with 9 paid holidays and 2 paid personal days Leadership and development opportunities Promotional opportunities About the Role: The Rockhurst University Department of Safety and Security is seeking a dedicated, community-minded Armed Patrol Officer to join our Uniformed Patrol Division on the evening/overnight shift. As a commission-based Patrol Agent (Class A Private Officer License under Missouri Title 17 & Chapter 84), you will hold full authority to deter, prevent, and respond to incidents—maintaining a safe, welcoming environment for our 3,000 students, faculty, and campus visitors. Essential Functions: Campus & Neighborhood Patrol: Conduct foot, bicycle, golf cart, and vehicle patrols across campus and surrounding university areas. Community Engagement: Build positive relationships with students, staff, and visitors using modern Community-Oriented Policing techniques. Public Safety & Emergency Response: Rapidly respond to emergency and non-emergency calls, alarms, and safety requests. Safety Escorts & Facility Security: Provide safety escorts for students and staff; locking and unlocking university facilities. Investigations & Reporting: Conduct thorough criminal and internal investigations; complete clear accurate incident reports. What We’re Looking For Minimum Qualifications: Age & Education: 21+ years of age with a High School Diploma or GED. Licensing: Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Commissioning: Must qualify for (or currently hold) an Armed Private Officer License through the Kansas City, Missouri Police Department within 45 days of hire (and maintain annually). Certifications: CPR/AED and Basic First Aid certified (or ability to obtain upon hire). Skills: Excellent communication and customer service skills; intermediate computer proficiency (MS Office, Teams, Outlook). Ability to pass a written exam, oral interview, comprehensive background investigation, physical exam, and drug screen. Preferred Experience: Prior experience in Law Enforcement, Campus Safety, Military, or Armed Security. How to Apply: Ready to make a difference and invest in your future? Please submit your Resume, Cover Letter, and Contact Information for Three (3) Professional References through our official online portal. Note: Applications submitted via email, regular mail, or in-person walk-ins cannot be accepted. All candidates must apply online. Disclaimer : This job posting summarizes the general nature and level of work expected for this role. It is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications. Rockhurst University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and uses E-Verify. Rockhurst is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive work environment and recruits without regard to race, religion, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, or disability. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States (visa sponsorship is not available). Share job details to About ROCKHURST UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
